 The Vim plugins in the "compiler" directory will set options to use the
 selected compiler.  For `:compiler` local options are set, for `:compiler!`
 global options.
+
+In normal use, select a compiler with `:compiler {name}` and then run
+|:make|.  The compiler plugin usually sets 'makeprg' and 'errorformat' so
+Vim can run the compiler and read its messages.  The descriptions below
+document options for particular compiler plugins.
+
+The values set by a compiler plugin can be changed afterwards with |:set| or
+|:setlocal|.  `:compiler {name}` sets options for the current buffer, while
+`:compiler! {name}` sets global options; a buffer-local value takes precedence
+over a global value.
+
